{"metric":"photon_rocket","source":[{"metric":"photon_rocket","system":"rectilinear","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"f9145a4cb8e7b97e"},{"metric":"photon_rocket","system":"robinson_trautman","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"c6734e01349c733d"},{"metric":"schwarzschild","system":"eddington_finkelstein_outgoing","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"8bfce6914f41a1cf"}],"views":[{"id":"behind","label":"Behind the rocket","box":[-1.8708,3.4416,-1.8708,1.8708],"input":"A burn from $u = 0$ to $cu = 10\\,m_0$ along the first axis, with the acceleration $\\alpha = 2\\sin^2(\\pi cu/10m_0)/(25\\,m_0)$ and the rapidity $w = \\int\\alpha\\,c\\,du$, which ends at $2/5$, a speed of $0.38\\,c$. The mass is $m = m_0e^{-3w}$ from the mass $m_0$ at the start, the least loss that keeps the density of the radiation positive in every direction, and ends at $0.30\\,m_0$.","settings":"$m_0$, the mass before the burn, is the unit of every length and of $cu$.","restriction":"The half of the axis of flight behind the rocket, $\\theta = 0$ in its rest frame, a totally geodesic surface, each point in the diagram a single event; off the axis the light rays of fixed $\\theta$ and $\\phi$ are turned out of their plane during the burn.","caption":["The half of the axis behind the rocket through the declared burn, each point in the diagram a single event. The outgoing rays, one for each retarded time, are $p = -\\arctan e^{-(cu - 5m_0)/5m_0}$, and an ingoing ray keeps one $q$. A ray that comes in from $\\mathscr{I}^-$ with the advanced time $v$ of Schwarzschild's exterior before the burn has $q = \\arctan e^{(cv - 15m_0)/10m_0}$, and a ray that leaves the singularity at the retarded time $u_0$ has $q = -\\pi/2 - p(u_0)$, which puts $r = 0$ on the straight line $T = -\\pi/2$.","The singularity lies in the past, a white hole, and the past horizon $q = 0$ divides the light that left it from the light that came in from $\\mathscr{I}^-$. Before the burn that horizon is $r = 2m_0$. As the rocket loses mass the lines of constant $r$ between $0.60\\,m_0$ and $2m_0$, spacelike inside the white hole, turn timelike, and after the burn the plane is Schwarzschild's of the mass $0.30\\,m_0$, whose horizon $r = 2m$ is the edge $u = \\infty$. During the burn the lines of constant $r$ beyond the second zero of $g^{rr}$, which comes in to $4.73\\,m_0$, are spacelike: a ray sent after the rocket from there gains $r$."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[1.5708,-1.5708],[3.1416,0.0],[1.5708,1.5708],[-1.5708,-1.5708]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[1.5708,-1.5708],[3.1416,0.0],[1.5708,1.5708],[-1.5708,-1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[1.5708,-1.5708],[0.3621,-1.5649],[-0.5965,-1.5531],[-0.9061,-1.5566],[-1.5708,-1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[1.5708,-1.5708],[0.3901,-1.5448],[0.1048,-1.5287],[-0.1289,-1.5043],[-0.3049,-1.4728],[-0.3767,-1.4542],[-0.4412,-1.4324],[-0.4978,-1.4074],[-0.5465,-1.3793],[-0.6481,-1.3011],[-0.6979,-1.2697],[-0.751,-1.2491],[-0.803,-1.2431],[-0.839,-1.2462],[-0.8843,-1.2561],[-0.9402,-1.2746],[-1.0055,-1.3011],[-1.2452,-1.4109],[-1.5708,-1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[1.5708,-1.5708],[1.1155,-1.5369],[0.5701,-1.5013],[0.3916,-1.48],[0.2491,-1.451],[0.1787,-1.4298],[0.1135,-1.4029],[0.0607,-1.3724],[0.0201,-1.3389],[-0.0125,-1.2985],[-0.0336,-1.256],[-0.0465,-1.2067],[-0.0509,-1.1506],[-0.0446,-1.0712],[-0.0257,-0.9823],[0.0024,-0.894],[0.044,-0.795],[0.114,-0.6645],[0.1965,-0.536],[0.3077,-0.3859],[0.4226,-0.2548],[0.4518,-0.2124],[0.4772,-0.1678],[0.5042,-0.1088],[0.528,-0.0438],[0.6104,0.2386],[0.6578,0.3754],[0.7195,0.516],[0.7925,0.6506],[0.8475,0.7386],[0.9113,0.8312],[0.9831,0.927],[1.0878,1.056],[1.1959,1.18],[1.2984,1.2916],[1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[1.5708,